SUMMARY:2 hour Spirited Improv Community Playshop
DESCRIPTION:Awakening Asheville\n### SPIRITED IMPROV Community Playshop:\n
 \nThis is not traditional improvisation. Imagine Spirited Improv as a spir
 itual practice\, where creativity meets consciousness and community. No ex
 perience necessary.\n\n**ABOUT SPIRITED IMPROV**\n\nSpirited Improv is a u
 nique fusion of expressive arts\, spiritual practice\, and group play that
  helps you release fear\, trust the unknown\, and show up as your truest s
 elf.\nSpirited Improv is a soul-centered community experience that uses im
 provisational play as the container for spiritual growth\, personal transf
 ormation\, and authentic connection. Rather than focusing on comedy or per
 formance\, we use improv as a living practice\, one that invites presence\
 , trust\, curiosity\, and responsiveness in the moment.\n\nFacilitated by 
 Jessica Chilton\, who brings over 20 years of improvisational performing a
 rts experience and 16 years as an expressive arts therapist\, weaving crea
 tivity\, spirituality\, and presence into a safe\, transformative group ex
 perience.\n\n**2 HR COMMUNITY PLAYSHOP**\nThis special session takes place
  on the final day of the current Spirited Improv series\, when we open the
  experience to the wider community.\nYou’ll join the participants who ha
 ve been playing together throughout the series. You’re welcome to watch 
 from the audience and enjoy the unfolding experience\, or jump in and part
 icipate in the improvisational play alongside the group.\n\nThis is a beau
 tiful way to experience Spirited Improv before joining a future series.\n\
 n**WHAT PAST PARTICIPANTS ARE SAYING**\n\n“Spirited Improv is authentic\
 , vulnerable and connective. It meets my need to deeply feel\, be seen and
  see others. On my first night I experienced such a profound healing exper
 ience after sharing what was on my heart. It was like a sound\, healing to
 uch\, full moon energy bath that opened my heart. ” \\~ Kate\n\n“Spiri
 ted Improv is a fun and little bit edgy way of interacting with the myster
 y of the moment. You decide how much you want to interact or observe from 
 the audience so you never have to do anything you don't want to do. It is 
 an opportunity to let go of control and explore the spontaneity of life an
 d creativity in a supportive\, safe environment..” \\~ Kenyon\n\n“I go
 t to play\, move my body\, laugh\, take joy in watching my friends come al
 ive\, give and receive big hugs\, and feel the presence of the ancestors w
 ho always join me. There’s something so sacred about being present with 
 others while we play\, witness and embody what is.” \\~ Sue\n\n$$$PAY WH
 AT YOU WANT OPTION $$$\n\nMore info at https://spiritedimprov.com
